// kabi_rule! type pins. GENERATED, not hand-captured: every tag below is what
// gendwarfksyms emits (--stable --symtypes) for the closure of the 19
// exports, read from each build's own pristine-C reference object
// (BUILD/abi-ref/lib/string_helpers.o) by rig/kabi-pin-variants.py. A tag
// whose text is identical in every variant is unconditional; a tag that
// differs (task_struct, file, device, ... -- they vary by Kconfig AND by
// ARCH: logs/arm64.md failure 7) sits in a `mod` keyed on
// target_arch + CONFIG_VMCORE_INFO, this project's existing discriminant for
// "which of our Kconfig families is this" (lib/buildid_rs.rs,
// logs/porting-hazards.md "config-keyed pins"). The module names list the
// variants that carry each text; a variant that never references a tag is a
// don't-care and shares the first text.
// TO ADD A VARIANT (riscv64, a third Kconfig family): build it, run
// rig/abi-ref.sh on it, add the arch line in variant() of the script (riscv64 done 2026-10-04; its fast/full discriminant is DISC in the script, not VMCORE_INFO), rerun:
//   rig/kabi-pin-variants.py --apply port/tree/lib/string_helpers_rs.rs \
//       build-fast build-full build-arm64 build-arm64-full [build-riscv64]
// then rig/kabi-contract-check.sh on EVERY build must say 0 DIFFER.
// A variant with no pins here fails the check loudly (CRC differs), never
// silently.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
